%N A401668 Number of groups G of order n such that |Aut(G)| = n.
%C A401668 a(n) >= 1 if n = 1, or n = 2^m with m >= 3 (G = C_(2^(m-1)) X C_2), or n = 4*3^k with k >= 1 (G = C_2 X C_2 X C_(3^k)), or n = p*t*(p-1) where p is an odd prime and every prime factor of t divides p-1 (G = C_p : C_(t*(p-1)), the cyclic group acting through a generator of Aut(C_p)); examples are n = 6, 12, 20, 24, 40, 42, 84, 110.
%C A401668 For G = C_p : C_(t*(p-1)) as above: every automorphism has the form a -> a^u, b -> a^v*b^w with u in (Z/p)*, v in Z/p and w = 1 + (p-1)*j, 0 <= j < t, gcd(w, t) = 1. All t values of w are admissible if and only if every prime factor of t divides p-1, and then |Aut(G)| = p*(p-1)*t = |G|.
%C A401668 a(2^m) >= 3 for m >= 4: besides C_(2^(m-1)) X C_2, the modular group C_(2^(m-1)) : C_2 qualifies (m >= 4), and a third group qualifies (m = 4, 5: found by computer; m >= 6: see next comment).
%C A401668 Proof for the third group, m >= 6, N = 2^(m-2): let H = <a> X <d> = C_N X C_2 and let beta be the automorphism of H of order 2 with beta(a) = a^(1+N/4)*d, beta(d) = d*a^(N/2); G = H : <b>, b acting as beta, |G| = 2^m. With c = [a,b], G has the presentation <a,b | a^N = b^2 = 1, [c,a] = 1, c^2 = a^(N/2), b*c*b = c^(-1)>, so Aut(G) corresponds to the pairs (x,y) of G satisfying these relations and generating G. Phi(G) = {a^i*d^j : i even} has index 4; y must be one of the 4 involutions outside H and x = a^i*d^j*b^k with i odd. For k = 0 all 4*N such pairs satisfy the relations; for k = 1 the commutator [x,y] does not commute with x. Hence |Aut(G)| = 4*N = 2^m. G is nonabelian of exponent 2^(m-2), so it differs from the other two groups.
%H A401668 Sajid Khan Hussain, <a href="/A401668/b401668.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..255</a>
%e A401668 a(6) = 1: S_3 has Aut(S_3) = S_3 of order 6, while |Aut(C_6)| = 2.
%e A401668 a(8) = 2: Aut(C_4 X C_2) = Aut(D_8) = D_8, of order 8. The other groups of order 8 do not qualify: |Aut(C_8)| = 4, |Aut(C_2^3)| = 168 and |Aut(Q_8)| = 24.
%o A401668 (GAP) LoadPackage("smallgrp"); LoadPackage("autpgrp");
%o A401668 a := function(n) local c, i, G, s; c := 0; for i in [1..NrSmallGroups(n)] do G := SmallGroup(n, i); if Size(G) = 1 then s := 1; elif IsPGroup(G) then s := AutomorphismGroupPGroup(G).size; else s := Size(AutomorphismGroup(G)); fi; if s = n then c := c + 1; fi; od; return c; end;
%o A401668 List([1..100], a);
%Y A401668 Cf. A000001 (number of groups of order n), A000688 (number of abelian groups of order n), A060689 (number of nonabelian groups of order n).
%Y A401668 Cf. A341825 (number of finite groups G with |Aut(G)| = n).
%K A401668 nonn,new
%O A401668 1,8
%A A401668 _Sajid Khan Hussain_, Nov 01 2026
